A||N||11||FieroJoe||Decklid Release Wiring||||1||
Z||000000||FieroJoe||01-17-2001||09:37 AM||||Im going to put in a decklid release setup, I have everything that's needed.  My car's already wired for it, up until the connector thats on the right hinge.  The wire from the switch is in the connector on the engine side, but is missing on the decklid side.  I was hoping to just run the wire from the connector up to the solenoid, so it can plug right into the existing wiring.  Any tips on how I can add the wire into that connector, so I can just plug it in?<P>TIA<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||01-17-2001||07:16 PM||||Read the trunk article in options & projects in my cave--&gt; <A HREF="http://fierocave.shorturl.com" TARGET=_blank>The Fiero Cave</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||01-17-2001||09:57 PM||||Unfortunatly, I dont have the harness from the donor car, otherwise every question that I have could have been answered by the Fiero Cave.  I bought the parts from some guy.  I dont know if I explained what I am looking to do well enough, I will try to get some pictures tomorrow.<P>Thanks though!||||reg||1
